Z||000017||FLASHY||05-05-2001||04:16 AM||||The last time I was in Las Vegas I saw taxi mini-vans with hub caps that didn't spin with the wheels. They put advertisements on them, so as they drive by you notice the darn things just sitting still...and then read the ad. It worked for me. Everytime I saw one I felt I had to read what it said. The wierd thing about it is the vans look like they are sliding on the wheels instead of rolling on them. Very trippy.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Songman||05-05-2001||11:17 PM||||It's not all that hard to do at all... Take a look at any semi next time you are going down the interstate. Almost all of them have one center that doesn't turn and as a matter of fact, it registers revolutions and works like an odometer as well..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
